      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-78297",
        "knowledge_point_id": "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix",
        "problem": "Which of the following represents a reflection across the $x$-axis?",
        "worked_solution": "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067709/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067709/assets/b93bb91dae85a3e3b40a8d0ade3d4f420064aaa6926431fa7f664c977bb8fd59.png)",
